{
  "platform_id": "y3giKIuJjDk",
  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:y3giKIuJjDk",
    "purpose": "A ranking of the waxed jackets that viewers voted as the internet's favourite, with background on waxed canvas and a look at each jacket's build, fit, features and price.",
    "video_type": "ranking",
    "thesis": "Waxed jackets are everywhere now. Tallying viewer votes and examining each jacket shows what makes the most-loved ones popular, chiefly fit, comfort and versatility, with Barbour taking the most votes.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Waxed cotton grew out of sailors oiling sails and clothing (oilskins). John Barbour brought it to farmers and countrymen.",
      "Eight jackets in the first half (Devium, Ginew, Tom Beckbe, Iron & Resin, Dehen 1920 Crissman) got votes but did not rank officially.",
      "Vote ranking: Bradley Mountain, Rogue Territory Supply Jacket (27% of votes), Freenote Cloth Riders Jacket (38 votes), Filson (65), Flint and Tinder Waxed Trucker (96), Barbour (186).",
      "The Filson section covers the sleeve vent and cuff design, the move to Bangladesh manufacturing and pricing, and an older 12.5 oz fabric that feels heavier than the current 14 oz.",
      "Fabric weight can be measured per linear yard or per square yard, so stated ounces are not directly comparable.",
      "The Flint and Tinder segment is sponsored by Huckberry and covers its fit, lining, US manufacturing and $300 price.",
      "The Barbour section covers its lightweight 6 oz Sylkoil fabric, room for layering, and features such as the throat latch, hood snaps, storm cuffs, vents and add-on liners."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "History of the sleeve vent",
        "summary": "Explains the sleeve opening that shirt-derived jackets like the Filson Cruiser inherited, and Filson's extra-fabric cut that blocks wind and rain.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Origins of wax canvas",
        "summary": "A brief history: sailors oiling sails and clothes with linseed oil and paraffin (oilskins), John Barbour bringing it to countrymen, and waxed cotton's spread. Explains how viewer votes were gathered.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Devium Overdrive jacket",
        "summary": "The made-in-USA Devium Overdrive waxed jacket: 9 and 12 oz canvas, build quality, wide chest and back with a back pleat, and suitability for many climates.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Ginew Legends Rider jacket",
        "summary": "Ginew's background as a Native American-owned denim brand, the story behind the motorcycle-inspired Legends Rider jacket, its price with an email discount, its build, and its Pendleton jacquard lining, with Pendleton history.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Tom Beckbe jacket features",
        "summary": "The Tom Beckbe Tensaw: the founder's hunting background, the large back and arm gussets that allow layering, and utility features like bellowed pockets, adjustable cuffs, two-way zip and storm flap. Brief mention of the Shallowford.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 14
      },
      {
        "title": "Iron and Resin overview",
        "summary": "Iron & Resin's motorcycle focus: the Scout and Cruiser jackets, waterproof linings, Halley Stevensons fabric, overseas manufacturing and value, and a slimmer 'California cut'.",
        "first_segment": 14,
        "last_segment": 17
      },
      {
        "title": "Crissman overshirt",
        "summary": "The Dehen 1920 Crissman waxed overshirt, which the creator long doubted would suit him, and how it suits cold, wet, windy weather.",
        "first_segment": 17,
        "last_segment": 19
      },
      {
        "title": "Bradley Mountain cabin jacket",
        "summary": "Start of the official voting ranking. Shows the Bradley Mountain Wilder anniversary backpack as an example of the brand's overbuilt style and describes the Cabin waxed jacket's short sleeves and wide back.",
        "first_segment": 19,
        "last_segment": 20
      },
      {
        "title": "Rogue Territory Supply Jacket",
        "summary": "27% of votes. Its celebrity wearers, plain unlined minimal design, watch-chain detail, and thoughts on lined versus unlined waxed jackets.",
        "first_segment": 21,
        "last_segment": 23
      },
      {
        "title": "Freenote Cloth Riders Jacket",
        "summary": "38 votes. Its famous wearers, Freenote Cloth as an American heritage brand, elasticated back gussets, and the idea of an everyday signature jacket.",
        "first_segment": 23,
        "last_segment": 25
      },
      {
        "title": "Filson jacket analysis",
        "summary": "65 votes. The creator's own Filson Tin Cloth Cruiser, fit, the move from US to Bangladesh manufacturing and pricing, old versus new fabric weights (linear vs square yard), double-layer cuffs, and vintage Mackinaw-style cruisers.",
        "first_segment": 25,
        "last_segment": 31
      },
      {
        "title": "Flint and Tinder trucker",
        "summary": "Sponsored segment, 96 votes. Huckberry's Flint and Tinder Waxed Trucker as worn by Pedro Pascal in The Last of Us: fit, longer sleeves, lining, wool-lined version, US-made Martexin fabric, and $300 price.",
        "first_segment": 31,
        "last_segment": 34
      },
      {
        "title": "Barbour jacket review",
        "summary": "The top pick with 186 votes. Barbour's lightweight 6 oz Sylkoil fabric, room for layering, throat latch, hood snaps, storm cuffs, vents and interchangeable liners.",
        "first_segment": 34,
        "last_segment": 37
      }
    ],
